{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZHexagon","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagon","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy","lean:module:QOU.Mass.KZHolonomy.FlatTransport"],"declarations":46,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagon.hexagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagon.hexagon","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagon.lean#L313-L532","doc":"**The hexagon relation for the KZ associator.**  With `C = −A − B` and `A`, `B`, `C`\nnon-resonant, `e^{−iπA} Φ(C,A) e^{−iπC} Φ(B,C) e^{−iπB} Φ(A,B) = 1`.\n\nSix solutions of `KZ(A,B)` (the normalised solutions at `0` and `1` of `KZ(A,B)`, `KZ(B,C)`,\n`KZ(C,A)`, pulled back along the order-three rotation `z ↦ 1 − 1/z`) are compared in turn\naround the fixed point `e^{iπ/3}`; consecutive ones differ by an associator or by a\nhalf-monodromy, and going once around returns the first one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagon.normSq_gt_of_lin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagon.normSq_gt_of_lin","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagon.lean#L310-L311","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagon.mem_Dh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagon.mem_Dh","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHexagon.lean#L307-L308","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHexagon.isOpen_Dh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHexagon.isOpen_Dh","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-obs